; expect 7
; An application whose HEAD is not a name. The head dispatch had no
; arm for it and wrote the constant 0, which does not emit a wrong
; call - it DELETES the application. A non-name head is evaluated as a
; value and applied one argument at a time.
(:: main Int)

(fn (main)
  ((lambda (x) x)
    7
  )
)
